; Hit test of an entity against the player, then continue where the caller says
;
; Used by the enemy handlers (Death, Satan, the crusaders and the other entities), which JP here with their slot on the
; stack: SP points at the slot's two hit box words (+$C offset, +$E far corner; both words have y in the low byte and x
; in the high byte, in 2-pixel units, see #R$C100). The minimum corner of the entity's box is its position plus the
; offset, the maximum corner its position plus the far corner word (measured from the position, not from the offset
; corner: it is a size only while the offset is 0). The two corners go to DE and BC and the code falls into the overlap
; test #R$A85F with IX = #R$A87A. HL is stored as the operand of the JP at #R$A880, so that #R$A87A goes on at the
; caller's address with SP just after the two words.
; .
; Hardware: none.
;
; DE Position of the entity: D = x, E = y (2-pixel units)
; HL Address to continue at after the test
; SP Slot address + $C (the hit box offset word)
@label=HitTest
@isub=LD (SmcHitContinue+1),HL
c$A851 LD ($A881),HL ; continuation address
 $A854 POP HL        ; hit box offset (y, x)
 $A855 ADD HL,DE     ; minimum corner = position + offset
 $A856 EX DE,HL      ; DE = minimum corner
 $A857 POP BC        ; hit box far corner (y, x)
 $A858 ADD HL,BC     ; maximum corner = position + far corner
 $A859 LD B,H        ; BC = maximum corner
 $A85A LD C,L        ;
 $A85B LD IX,$A87A   ; continue at #R$A87A after the test
